// src/elevate.pdx — mount.pdxfs.M1-001 (scaffold) — elevate-channel
// placeholder, real body at M3-001.
//
// design/tooling/volume-tooling-ux.md §4.2 defines a mount-point-class
// table gating whether mount.pdxfs must request elevation via
// KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL before calling sys_mount:
//
//   /system/**          -- always elevate
//   /boot/**            -- always elevate
//   /dev/**             -- always elevate
//   /mnt/**             -- never
//   /home/<$user>/**    -- never (own subtree)
//   /home/<$other>/**   -- founder-only elevate
//   /tmp/**             -- never
//   anywhere else       -- founder-only elevate (conservative default)
//
// None of that table, and no libpdx-elevate call, exists at M1.
// mount.pdxfs.M1-003's own dry-run happy path never inspects
// <mount-point>'s class -- the --dry-run print always succeeds
// regardless of where the caller points it, and the non-dry-run branch
// is an unconditional "not yet implemented" exit 1 (src/main.pdx) that
// never reaches any elevate decision either. This file is therefore a
// SCAFFOLD, matching mkfs.pdxfs's own "STUB for M1, real body at a
// later milestone" posture for src/target.pdx.
//
// libpdx-elevate availability note: as of this landing, a
// `grep -rl libpdx-elevate` across the paideia-os monorepo and every
// repo under paideia-satellites/ finds ZERO implementation files --
// the same "design-doc-mentioned, not yet bootstrapped" status
// mkfs.pdxfs.M1-002's own design/architecture.md §3 documents for
// libpdx-argv (which mount.pdxfs's own src/argv.pdx also works around
// with a minimal inline parser). elevate_needed below is written to be
// the same shape (a path-classifying query in, a boolean decision out)
// a future libpdx-elevate-backed rewrite would present, so a caller
// added at M3-001 does not need an ABI change when a real
// classification table and a real KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL request/response
// round-trip replace this stub's body.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
// M1 stub contract
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// elevate_needed ALWAYS returns 0 (not required), regardless of its
// mount_point_ptr argument -- it does not read a single byte of that
// string yet. This is deliberately the most permissive possible
// answer: since no code path in this landing calls sys_mount (the only
// operation elevation would ever gate), a stub that always says
// "elevation not required" cannot cause a M1 caller to skip a real
// safety check that exists nowhere in this repo yet. The mount-point-
// class table and the real KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL request/response
// exchange are mount.pdxfs.M3-001.
//
// Not called by any M1 code path (src/main.pdx's _start never
// references this module) -- it exists at M1 purely to reserve the
// call-site shape M3-001 will wire in, per this issue's own file-list
// instruction ("elevate.pdx -- placeholder for elevate-channel logic
// (M2+)").
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
// Encoder-gap discipline
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// No `add reg, [mem]` anywhere. No `test` mnemonic; every zero-check is
// `cmp reg, 0`. Reserved-label discipline: not applicable yet -- this
// stub's one function has no internal branch, hence no label to
// prefix; a future real body's labels will use the `mount_elevate_`
// prefix, matching this repo's other three files' per-file prefix
// convention.
//
// Upstream: design/tooling/volume-tooling-ux.md §4.2 (paideia-os).

module Elevate = structure {

  // --- elevate_needed return values. --------------------------------------
  pub let ELEVATE_NOT_REQUIRED : u64 = 0
  pub let ELEVATE_REQUIRED     : u64 = 1

  // ==========================================================================
  // elevate_needed(mount_point_ptr) -> u64 (ELEVATE_NOT_REQUIRED | ELEVATE_REQUIRED)
  //
  // mount_point_ptr in rdi: a NUL-terminated <mount-point> string,
  // typically ParsedArgv.mount_point_ptr from Argv::argv_parse. M1
  // STUB: unconditionally returns ELEVATE_NOT_REQUIRED without
  // inspecting mount_point_ptr at all -- see module header for why this
  // is a safe default at M1 (no caller anywhere in this repo yet uses
  // the result to gate a real sys_mount call). The real mount-point-
  // class classification (§4.2's table: /system, /boot, /dev always
  // elevate; /home/<other> and the conservative default are
  // founder-only elevate; everything else never elevates) is
  // mount.pdxfs.M3-001.
  //
  // Pure leaf: rax/rdi are SysV caller-save; no push/pop, no nested
  // call, no branch.
  // ==========================================================================
  pub let elevate_needed : (u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (mount_point_ptr: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "mount.pdxfs.M1-001 (scaffold): elevate_needed entry point, an M2+ placeholder per this issue's own file-list instruction. mount_point_ptr arrives in rdi but is never dereferenced or otherwise inspected -- the M1 stub body is exactly `xor rax, rax; ret`, unconditionally returning ELEVATE_NOT_REQUIRED (0) regardless of the argument. This is safe at M1 because no caller anywhere in this repo (src/main.pdx's _start included) invokes this function or uses any elevate decision to gate a real sys_mount call -- the real mount-point-class table (§4.2) and the KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL request/response round-trip this function will eventually wrap are mount.pdxfs.M3-001. Declared `effects: {mem}` (matching every other leaf helper in this repo's module-level convention) even though this stub body touches no memory -- the real M3-001 body will need to read mount_point_ptr's bytes, and keeping the effect annotation stable now avoids a signature churn at that milestone. Pure leaf -- rax/rdi are SysV caller-save, no push/pop, no branch, hence no label to prefix.",
      block: {
        xor rax, rax;
        ret;
      }
    }
}
